.tsx (ChatArea first-send flow with conversationId + location.state.initialMessage, rendered under React.StrictMode); fix lands in the conversationId-reset effect of app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts","then":"on the unchanged tree the acceptance test fails red with exactly 'expected true to be false // Object.is equality' (the captured signal is observed aborted — StrictMode's second pass of the conversationId-reset effect aborts the just-started stream and swallows the AbortError as intentional); after the fix the captured AbortSignal.aborted is false, the button with aria-label 'Stop response' (app/frontend/src/components/ChatInput.tsx:122) is visible while the stream is in flight, and the assistant text renders once [DONE] arrives","when":"the initial message is dispatched and the mocked SSE stream is held in flight and then completed with [DONE]"},{"given":"a stream is in flight on conversation 'conv-a' (startStream called against a never-resolving or gated mocked fetch)","id":"AC-2","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts#useStreamingResponse (conversationId-reset effect)","then":"the old stream's AbortSignal aborts and all streaming state clears (isStreaming false, streamingContent '', streamingSources [], streamingStatus null) — kept behaviour, pinned today by the 'resets all streaming state when conversationId changes' tests in app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.test.ts:467-508","when":"the conversation id changes from 'conv-a' to 'conv-b' (the real conversation-switch navigation /c/a → /c/b)"},{"given":"a stream is in flight on conversation 'conv-a'","id":"AC-3","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/hooks/useStreamingResponse.ts#useStreamingResponse (conversationId-reset effect)","then":"the stream is not aborted and streaming state is untouched (isStreaming stays true, tokens keep accumulating) — kept behaviour pinned today by 'does not reset state when conversationId stays the same' (useStreamingRespon