rontend)."],"issue":{"number":103,"title":"fix(chat): first message's stream is aborted by StrictMode's effect re-run, nothing renders"},"out_of_scope":["Any change to the SSE format, app/frontend/src/lib/api.ts, or the backend (explicit issue exclusion).","Removing or conditionally disabling React.StrictMode in app/frontend/src/main.tsx — that would mask the symptom instead of making the stream survive the effect re-run.","The useMessages.ts StrictMode second-pass duplicate GET and its late-resolving setMessages overwrite risk (investigation 'nearby oddity') — not implicated in the reported symptom; separate issue.","The e2e harness (harness/e2e.py) and the browser journey — evidence only; the fix is verified by the new Vitest acceptance tests plus the existing suites.","Retry, rate-limit (429/RateLimitError), citation rendering, or any other ChatArea send-path behaviour beyond the reset/abort timing."],"risks":["Only the abort-signal assertion is reliably red on current main: with a mocked fetch that ignores its signal, the reader keeps yielding after the abort, so 'Stop response visible' and 'assistant text renders after [DONE]' can each pass on broken code if asserted after completion — the red checkpoint must assert the captured signal (expect(signal.aborted).toBe(false)) to produce the pinned symptom 'expected true to be false // Object.is equality'.","The 'Stop response' mid-stream assertion needs a gated SSE body (withhold [DONE] until the assertion is made) so the in-flight state is observable; asserting after the stream finished races and may not reproduce the symptom.","StrictMode double-invokes mount effects synchronously within one commit on React 18.3.1 + @testing-library/react 16 (jsdom); the test must rely on that ordering rather than fake timers, and the send-effect's dispatchedInitialRef guard means only the reset effect's second pass can abort — the test should not re-dispatch the send.","If the fix moves the reset into the send path (ChatArea) in